//
// Two slots: the geometry, and the two direct call sites it requires.
//
// Everything ping-pong needs that can be checked without hardware. The
// hardware half needs a mechanism that does not exist yet, and this test is
// what pins the parts that do.
//
// Program memory is 0x4000 with a 0x2000 write granule, so there are exactly
// two granules and the two slots take one each. That is forced, not chosen:
// while either slot is written the core must be executing from the other, since
// a write to the granule the core is fetching from is dropped about half the
// time. The Slot's core_in field records which granule the core is in during
// each write, and validate() checks it -- expressing the rule per slot rather
// than as "must not share with the resident at 0" is what makes ping-pong
// expressible at all. The stricter phrasing would rule it out by definition
// rather than by evidence.
//
// What is still missing is the dispatch path in the upper granule. The core
// returns from a slot into the resident, which lives at 0 -- so on the phase
// where granule 0 is being written, the core would be executing the granule
// being written. AIETargetLdScript.cpp emits a single `.text ... > program` and
// aiecc links with --orphan-handling=error, so a link_with fragment, which
// arrives as an INPUT(), cannot introduce a second output section to hold a
// copy. That needs either a write-once bootstrap overlay or named-section
// placement for core code.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/clang++ --target=aie2p-none-unknown-elf -O2 -c %S/../resident.cc -o %t/resident.o
//
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py geometry pingpong | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GEOM
// GEOM: write-granule 0x2000
// GEOM: slot b 0x2000 0x1c00
// GEOM-NEXT: slot a 0x400 0x1c00
// GEOM-NEXT: bootstrap stub 0x3c00 0x400
//
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py emit --recipe pingpong --slot-ld %t/slot.ld --phases 0,1 --out %t/d.mlir
//
// One symbol per slot: two slots cannot share a call site, because slot.ld
// supplies absolute addresses rather than a table, so an indirect call would
// have nothing to go through.
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LD --input-file=%t/slot.ld
// LD-DAG: overlay_entry_a = 0x400;
// LD-DAG: overlay_entry_b = 0x2000;
//
// RUN: cd %t && %aiecc --tmpdir=%t/p1 --get-xclbin --xclbin-name=%t/p1.xclbin --get-npu-insts --npu-insts-name=%t/p1.bin %t/d.mlir
//
// Both entries are absolute with no body, exactly as in the single-slot case.
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/llvm-readelf -s %t/p1/elfs_main_core_0_2/elfs_main_core_0_2.elf | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SYM
// SYM-DAG: 00000400 {{ *}}0 NOTYPE {{ *}}GLOBAL {{ *}}DEFAULT {{ *}}ABS overlay_entry_a
// SYM-DAG: 00002000 {{ *}}0 NOTYPE {{ *}}GLOBAL {{ *}}DEFAULT {{ *}}ABS overlay_entry_b
//
// And the phase loop really did unroll into two direct jumps, one per slot,
// rather than one call site reused.
// RUN: %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR/bin/llvm-objdump -d %t/p1/elfs_main_core_0_2/elfs_main_core_0_2.elf | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=JUMP
// JUMP-DAG: jl {{.*}}#0x400
// JUMP-DAG: jl {{.*}}#0x2000
//
// Payload writes alternate between the two slots: 0x20400 and 0x22000 are the
// host offset 0x20000 plus each slot's base.
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py workload --tag 1 --size 0x400 --output %t/w.o --workdir %t
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py link --object %t/w.o --resident %t/p1 --recipe pingpong --slot a --output %t/ovl_a.elf
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py link --object %t/w.o --resident %t/p1 --recipe pingpong --slot b --output %t/ovl_b.elf
// RUN: %python %S/../pm.py emit --recipe pingpong --phases 0,1 --payload %t/ovl_a.elf --payload %t/ovl_b.elf --out %t/d2.mlir
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ADDR --input-file=%t/d2.mlir
// ADDR-DAG: aiex.npu.blockwrite({{.*}}) {address = 132096 : ui32
// ADDR-DAG: aiex.npu.blockwrite({{.*}}) {address = 139264 : ui32
